 "customerTurns": 3,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "My Samsung dishwasher DW60M6050FS keeps showing 4C and beeping, won't do anything"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "4C on your Samsung means: Water supply issue - little/no fresh water enters (supply valve/frozen/clogged inlet). From what you have described, the most likely cause is water supply / isolation tap / inlet hose / inlet filter (check first). Check the tap the dishwasher hose connects to is fully on, the hose isn't kinked behind the machine, and if the hose has an AquaStop box at the tap end, whether its little window shows red. Was the tap off or the hose kinked (and is it sorted), does the AquaStop window show red or the hose look damaged, or is it all fine?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I checked the valve under the sink that the dishwasher is connected to. It's a screwdriver-slot type and the slot is at 90 degrees, so I think it's turned off. The hose has no kinks. Should I turn it on?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, you should turn the water supply valve back on. The 4C error code indicates a lack of water intake, which is likely caused by the valve being closed. Now turn the tap back on and start a programme. Does it fill normally now, or is it still not taking water?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, I've turned the valve on and started a programme. It's filling and running normally now. The plumber was working under the sink yesterday, so I guess he must have turned it off."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Good news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  }
 ],
